      ],
      "source": "https://www.cerescourier.com/news/local/museum-exhibits-highlight-ceres-from-its-inception/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The museum’s first exhibit, “From Amber Grain to Fruited Plain,” showcases original flour sacks from Daniel Whitmore’s 1880s mill, once a two‑year‑old operation that burned down.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cerescourier.com/news/local/museum-exhibits-highlight-ceres-from-its-inception/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1877 Steinway piano that once belonged to the Hiram Hughson family, founders of nearby Hughson, sits beside an organ donated by Aleene Landreth Landers in the museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cerescourier.com/news/local/museum-exhibits-highlight-ceres-from-its-inception/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Walter Perra, a native of Ceres, flew a P‑38 over enemy territory during World War II, helping disable railroads and supply lines for Allied forces.",
